1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,442
You can make an eighty-percent-smart decision today,

2
00:00:03,442 --> 00:00:05,494
watch it fail tomorrow morning,

3
00:00:05,494 --> 00:00:07,612
and ruin your future by assuming

4
00:00:07,612 --> 00:00:09,200
your strategy was wrong.

5
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:10,572
In Thinking in Bets,

6
00:00:10,572 --> 00:00:13,041
World Series of Poker champion Annie

7
00:00:13,041 --> 00:00:15,236
Duke warns against a mental trap

8
00:00:15,236 --> 00:00:16,403
called Resulting:

9
00:00:16,403 --> 00:00:18,666
judging the quality of a decision

10
00:00:18,666 --> 00:00:20,930
purely by its short-term outcome.

11
00:00:20,930 --> 00:00:23,465
Running a red light blindfolded and

12
00:00:23,465 --> 00:00:25,855
arriving home unharmed is still a

13
00:00:25,855 --> 00:00:27,158
terrible decision.

14
00:00:27,158 --> 00:00:27,810
Likewise,

15
00:00:27,810 --> 00:00:30,345
shipping a smart project that flops

16
00:00:30,345 --> 00:00:32,300
once can still be a winning

17
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:32,590
bet.

18
00:00:32,590 --> 00:00:33,546
Life is poker,

19
00:00:33,546 --> 00:00:34,229
not chess,

20
00:00:34,229 --> 00:00:36,891
because luck and hidden information sit

21
00:00:36,891 --> 00:00:37,915
at every table.

22
00:00:37,915 --> 00:00:40,646
Write down your reasoning beforehand and

23
00:00:40,646 --> 00:00:43,650
test positive-odds habits across fifty reps.

24
00:00:43,650 --> 00:00:46,669
Separate your daily process from single

25
00:00:46,669 --> 00:00:47,830
noisy outcomes,

26
00:00:47,830 --> 00:00:49,843
because in the real world,

27
00:00:49,843 --> 00:00:52,320
even when the math favors you...
